# Database rules (Supabase Postgres)

## Migrations
- One change per file in `supabase/migrations/`, named `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_short_description.sql`.
- Never edit an applied migration. Add a new one.
- Every migration starts with a comment block: purpose, tables touched, which prompt it belongs to.
- Wrap each migration so it can be read top to bottom: enums, then tables, then indexes, then functions, then triggers, then RLS policies.

## Tables
- Plural `snake_case` names. Every table has:
  - `id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid()` (except `profiles`, whose `id` references `auth.users(id) on delete cascade`)
  - `created_at timestamptz not null default now()`
  - `updated_at timestamptz not null default now()` maintained by the shared `set_updated_at()` trigger
- Use enums for fixed value sets (role, stream, status). Use foreign keys everywhere; add an index on every foreign key column.
- Text codes (F1, C3, content) are `unique` and `not null`.
- Skill names: `check (name ~ '^[a-z0-9-]{1,64}$' and name !~ '(claude|anthropic)')`.

## Row-level security (mandatory)
- `alter table ... enable row level security;` on every table in the same migration that creates it.
- Write separate policies for select, insert, update, delete. Name them plainly: `"learners read own lesson progress"`.
- Use the helper functions, never repeat role logic inline:
  - `public.current_app_role()` returns the signed-in user's role
  - `public.has_role(variadic roles app_role[])` returns boolean
  - `public.can_view_user(target uuid)` applies progress scope (self, department, all)
- Helper functions are `security definer`, `stable`, and set `search_path = ''` with fully qualified names (`public.profiles`).
- Reference data (departments, modules, domains, stages): any signed-in user may read; only trainer and admin may write.
- Learner-owned rows (progress, attempts, submissions): owner reads and inserts own; trainers read all; managers read via `can_view_user`; nobody updates another person's row except trainers through defined workflows.
- `profiles.role` and `profiles.progress_scope` may only be changed by admin. Enforce with a trigger, not just a policy, so a learner cannot promote themselves.
- Never grant anything to `anon` beyond what Supabase Auth itself needs.

## Audit
- Tables `profiles`, `placement_results`, `reviews`, `certificates`, `app_settings` get the shared `audit_row_change()` trigger writing to `audit_log` (actor, action, table, row id, before, after).

## Seed data
- `supabase/seed.sql` loads reference data only (departments, domains, stages, modules, module domains, department requirements, default settings, placeholder help pages). Source of truth: `docs/seed/curriculum_v1_1.json`. Never invent modules or change codes, weeks or hours.
- Seed must be safe to run twice (`on conflict (code) do update`).

## After any change
- Run `npx supabase db push` against the dev project only (never production unless Bharg says "production").
- Regenerate types: `npm run db:types`.
- Run the advisor check through the Supabase dashboard or MCP (security and performance) and fix any warnings about missing RLS or unindexed foreign keys.
